{"name":"Stinging Nettle","hex":"#495d39","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stinging nettle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A nettle; a member of any the species of genus Urtica, which cause painful short-term skin irritation, especially Urtica dioica, originally Eurasian, now naturalized elsewhere."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stinging_nettle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Urtica dioica","blocks":[{"text":"Urtica dioica, often known as common nettle, burn nettle, stinging nettle, nettle leaf, or just a nettle or stinger, is a herbaceous perennial flowering plant in the family Urticaceae. Originally native to Europe, much of temperate Asia and western North Africa, it is now found worldwide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Fen_nettle_%28Urtica_dioica_ssp._galeopsifolia%29_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5423125.jpg/330px-Fen_nettle_%28Urtica_dioica_ssp._galeopsifolia%29_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5423125.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urtica_dioica","wikidata":"Q155909"},{"title":"Urtica","blocks":[{"text":"Urtica is a genus of flowering plants in the family Urticaceae. Many species have stinging hairs and may be called nettles or stinging nettles. The generic name Urtica derives from the Latin for 'sting'."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Illustration_Urtica_dioica0.jpg/330px-Illustration_Urtica_dioica0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urtica","wikidata":"Q121671"},{"title":"List of plants known as nettle","blocks":[{"text":"Nettle refers to plants with stinging hairs, particularly those of the genus Urtica. It can also refer to plants which resemble Urtica species in appearance but do not have stinging hairs, such as dead nettle or false nettle listed below. Plants called \"nettle\" include:"},{"items":["Ball nettle – Solanum carolinense","Bull nettle\nCnidoscolus stimulosus, bull nettle, spurge nettle\nCnidoscolus texanus, Texas bull nettle\nCnidoscolus urens, bull nettle\nSolanum elaeagnifolium, bull nettle, silver-leaf nettle, white horse-nettle","Cnidoscolus stimulosus, bull nettle, spurge nettle","Cnidoscolus texanus, Texas bull nettle","Cnidoscolus urens, bull nettle","Solanum elaeagnifolium, bull nettle, silver-leaf nettle, white horse-nettle","Dead nettle, dumb nettle\nLamium, particularly Lamium album","Lamium, particularly Lamium album","False nettle – Boehmeria","Flame nettle – Coleus","Hedge nettle – Stachys","Hemp nettle – Galeopsis","Horse nettle:\nAgastache urticifolia – horse-nettle\nSolanum carolinense – ball-nettle, Carolina horse-nettle\nSolanum dimidiatum – western horse-nettle, robust horse-nettle\nSolanum elaeagnifolium – bull nettle, silver-leaf nettle, white horse-nettle\nSolanum rostratum – horse-nettle","Agastache urticifolia – horse-nettle","Solanum carolinense – ball-nettle, Carolina horse-nettle","Solanum dimidiatum – western horse-nettle, robust horse-nettle","Solanum elaeagnifolium – bull nettle, silver-leaf nettle, white horse-nettle","Solanum rostratum – horse-nettle","nettle tree or tree nettle:\nCeltis\nVarious species of the genus Dendrocnide\nUrera baccifera\nUrtica ferox","Celtis","Various species of the genus Dendrocnide","Urera baccifera","Urtica ferox","Nilgiri nettle, Himalayan giant nettle - Girardinia diversifolia","Painted nettle – Coleus scutellarioides","Rock nettle – Eucnide","Shiny-leaved nettle – Dendrocnide photiniphylla","Spurge nettle – Cnidoscolus","Stinging nettle\nHesperocnide\nmost, but not all subspecies of Urtica dioica\nUrtica gracilis\nUrtica incisa\nUrtica ferox","Hesperocnide","most, but not all subspecies of Urtica dioica","Urtica gracilis","Urtica incisa","Urtica ferox","Tree nettle - see nettle tree","White nettle\nLamium album\nPipturus argenteus","Lamium album","Pipturus argenteus","Wood nettle - Laportea canadensis"]},{"items":["Cnidoscolus stimulosus, bull nettle, spurge nettle","Cnidoscolus texanus, Texas bull nettle","Cnidoscolus urens, bull nettle","Solanum elaeagnifolium, bull nettle, silver-leaf nettle, white horse-nettle"]},{"items":["Lamium, particularly Lamium album"]},{"items":["Agastache urticifolia – horse-nettle","Solanum carolinense – ball-nettle, Carolina horse-nettle","Solanum dimidiatum – western horse-nettle, robust horse-nettle","Solanum elaeagnifolium – bull nettle, silver-leaf nettle, white horse-nettle","Solanum rostratum – horse-nettle"]},{"items":["Celtis","Various species of the genus Dendrocnide","Urera baccifera","Urtica ferox"]},{"items":["Hesperocnide","most, but not all subspecies of Urtica dioica","Urtica gracilis","Urtica incisa","Urtica ferox"]},{"items":["Lamium album","Pipturus argenteus"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_plants_known_as_nettle","wikidata":"Q16872290"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Fen_nettle_%28Urtica_dioica_ssp._galeopsifolia%29_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5423125.jpg/500px-Fen_nettle_%28Urtica_dioica_ssp._galeopsifolia%29_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5423125.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Fen_nettle_%28Urtica_dioica_ssp._galeopsifolia%29_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5423125.jpg/500px-Fen_nettle_%28Urtica_dioica_ssp._galeopsifolia%29_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5423125.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFen_nettle_(Urtica_dioica_ssp._galeopsifolia)_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5423125.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Urtica_dioica_specimen%2C_Cambridge_University_Botanic_Garden.jpg/250px-Urtica_dioica_specimen%2C_Cambridge_University_Botanic_Garden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimed